  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Strengthening of Civil Society Organisations facing the impact of extractive industries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This initiative aims to resolve conflicts related to water and land use through the promotion and application of the rights of access to information, citizen participation and access to justice contained in the LAC-P10 declaration and the Escazu Agreement.  The project is designed to strengthen advocacy actions in El Salvador  to complement wider efforts at regional level.  These include: a) Consultation processes with the participation of citizens and community organisations; b) Research on the impacts of oil palm and sugar cane monocultures on rights in the Central American region; c) Social media campaign will be launched linking the impacts of monocultures with the need to adhere to the Escaz&#xfa; agreement.</narrative>
  </description>
